From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: office <office@localhost>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] engine: a read-only session refuses every command that changes the workbook

docs/phase5/r6.md, owner 2026-11-08: a read-only session must not be changeable at all, not even for one frame. The engine gets
its own read-only state: `Session::read_only`. While it is set, `execute` refuses every command that changes the workbook before
it runs (`EngineError::Disabled`): every undoable command except the zoom commands (view only), and Undo, Redo, Cut, Edit Cell
(F2) and the Pen and Eraser tools. `commands()` reports them disabled. As a last resort inside the same call, a command that
nevertheless left a clean workbook dirty is put back (workbook, selection, calculation) with a `read-only safety net` warning
and an error, so no frame ever shows it. A host sets the flag; nothing changes while it is false. Unit test included.
---

diff --git a/crates/engine/src/cmd/mod.rs b/crates/engine/src/cmd/mod.rs
index 9404050..c81756e 100644
--- a/crates/engine/src/cmd/mod.rs
+++ b/crates/engine/src/cmd/mod.rs
@@ -61,7 +61,7 @@ pub struct CommandInfo {
 
 impl CommandSpec {
     pub fn info(&self, s: &Session) -> CommandInfo {
-        let e = (self.enabled)(s);
+        let e = (self.enabled)(s).and_then(|()| if s.read_only && refuses_when_read_only(self) { Err("read-only".into()) } else { Ok(()) });
         CommandInfo {
             id: self.id,
             label: self.label,
@@ -74,6 +74,16 @@ impl CommandSpec {
     }
 }
 
+/// Whether a read-only session ([`Session::read_only`]) refuses the command: every undoable one (they change the workbook; the
+/// zoom commands only change the view, which is saved with the file but is no edit) and the others that edit it or open an editor.
+pub fn refuses_when_read_only(c: &CommandSpec) -> bool {
+    match c.id {
+        "view.zoom" | "view.zoom100" | "view.zoomToSelection" => false,
+        "edit.undo" | "edit.redo" | "edit.cut" | "edit.beginEdit" | "draw.pen" | "draw.eraser" => true,
+        _ => c.undoable,
+    }
+}
+
 /// Params that hold a secret: `password`, or a name ending in `Password`.
 pub fn is_secret_param(key: &str) -> bool {
     key == "password" || key.ends_with("Password")
